1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Web3 has a compliance paradox.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:10,500
Traditional KYC makes you hand over your passport, your face, your home address — to databases that get hacked every week.

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:15,000
But fully anonymous DeFi? Shut down by regulators. You have to choose: expose your privacy, or break the law.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,500
And that's not the only problem. Compliance isn't static.

5
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:29,000
When someone lands on an OFAC sanctions list, revoking their access can take days — because it depends on manual, centralized updates.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,500
One point of failure. One too many.

7
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:40,000
ZK-CID fixes both halves of this broken system.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
ZK-CID: Zero-Knowledge Compliant Identity.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
We combine Decentralized Identity with Zero-Knowledge Proofs, so you can prove "I am compliant" — without ever revealing "who I am."

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Think of a nightclub: the bouncer knows you're over twenty-one. They just don't know your name, your birthday, or your ID number.

11
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:10,000
That's what we built for DeFi.

12
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Let's see it live. First, I generate an anonymous identity right here in the browser — my private key never leaves this device.

13
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Second, a trusted issuer verifies my documents off-chain, then adds my anonymous commitment to an on-chain Semaphore group.

14
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Now for the magic: I want into a regulated DeFi app, so I generate a Zero-Knowledge Proof right in the browser.

15
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:42,000
The math proves two things: I'm in the approved group, and I've never used this proof before. I submit it on-chain; the contract verifies it and mints my Access NFT.

16
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,000
I'm in — and the protocol never learned my identity.

17
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:58,000
And here's the part judges love: when a user hits a sanctions list, our Chainlink CRE workflow revokes their credential on-chain automatically — no humans, no delay.

18
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Watch: the revoked user tries to mint again — and gets rejected. Credential revoked. Done.

19
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Under the hood:

20
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Semaphore v4 for anonymous signaling, Solidity contracts on Hardhat, a Next.js frontend built on Scaffold-ETH 2 —

21
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:40,000
and Chainlink CRE for fully automated compliance lifecycle management. Every step is auditable on-chain, while privacy stays mathematically protected.

22
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:48,000
What does this unlock? Any DeFi protocol — a DEX, a lending platform — can plug into our gate and become regulatory-ready in a day.

23
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:56,000
They never touch user data, so they never own the legal risk. Regulators get verifiable compliance. Users get absolute privacy.

24
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Everybody wins.

25
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:10,000
This isn't just a hackathon project — it's the infrastructure compliant Web3 has been waiting for.

26
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Try it yourself: the live demo is live at web-3-0-decentralized.vercel.app, and the code is open source on GitHub.

27
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:24,000
I'm a solo developer building the trust layer for the next generation of DeFi.

28
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Thank you — and let's build a compliant, private Web3 together.
